BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:the-colorado-marathon-2027@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20261101T000000Z
DTSTART:20270502T063000Z
DTEND:20270502T103000Z
SUMMARY:The Colorado Marathon
DESCRIPTION:Annual Colorado Marathon in Fort Collins featuring scenic downhill courses through Poudre Canyon and Northern Colorado natural areas. Four distance options available. Known as one of Colorado's fastest races for Boston Marathon qualification. Event sells out quickly with vibrant community atmosphere.
LOCATION:301 Maple St. Fort Collins\, CO 80521 US
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ram-party-trail-runs-2027@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20261101T000000Z
DTSTART:20270515T060000Z
DTEND:20270515T100000Z
SUMMARY:Ram Party Trail Runs
DESCRIPTION:Ram Party Trail Runs features multiple distance options centered around the beautiful Rampart Reservoir in Woodland Park and Rampart Range Road. The race offers scenic views of Pikes Peak and the front range with elevation gains ranging from 3\,279 feet (60K) to 6\,964 feet (55 Mile).
LOCATION:Buffalo Lodge Bicycle Resort\, 2 El Paso Blvd\, Colorado Springs\, CO 80904
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:north-fork-50-2027@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20261101T000000Z
DTSTART:20270522T060000Z
DTEND:20270522T100000Z
SUMMARY:North Fork 50
DESCRIPTION:The North Fork 50 Mile/50K is an ultramarathon in the Colorado mountains southwest of Denver featuring 100% soft surface trails\, primarily singletrack through beautiful ponderosa pines and granite rock formations. The course includes sections through open burn areas from a 1996 fire. Race proceeds benefit the North Fork Volunteer Fire Department and local community organizations.
LOCATION:Buffalo Creek Clubhouse\, 18050 S Buffalo Creek Rd\, Buffalo Creek\, CO 80470
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:colorado-13er-2027@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20261101T000000Z
DTSTART:20270606T063000Z
DTEND:20270606T103000Z
SUMMARY:Colorado 13er
DESCRIPTION:The Colorado 13er is an exceptionally scenic\, looped half marathon (13.1 miles) that combines trail running and road racing through Louisville\, Colorado with spectacular views of the Flatirons. The course features 9 miles of flat\, crushed gravel with 10 water stations\, 5 port-a-john passes\, free parking\, and is chip-timed with live results. All participants receive a performance tee and finishers receive a collector's pint glass. Half marathon finishers also receive a collector's finisher medal. 5K and 10K options are available.
LOCATION:Home Depot\, 1200 Dillon Road\, Louisville\, CO 80027
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ring-the-springs-2027@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20261101T000000Z
DTSTART:20270619T060000Z
DTEND:20270619T100000Z
SUMMARY:Ring the Springs
DESCRIPTION:Ring the Springs is a trail running event featuring three distance options (100K\, 50K\, and 35K) through the stunning landscapes of Colorado Springs. The course weaves through majestic mountains\, scenic city parks\, and iconic landmarks including North Cheyenne Cañon and Pike National Forest trails. Starting and finishing at historic Rock Ledge Ranch in Garden of the Gods\, runners experience exhilarating climbs and rewarding descents while immersed in breathtaking mountain vistas.
LOCATION:Rock Ledge Ranch at Garden of The Gods\, 3105 Gateway Road\, Colorado Springs\, CO 80904
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:vail-hillclimb-2027@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20261101T000000Z
DTSTART:20270701T070000Z
DTEND:20270701T110000Z
SUMMARY:Vail HillClimb
DESCRIPTION:Vail Trail Running Series race taking place in July 2027 in Vail
LOCATION:Vail\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hardrock-100-2027@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20261101T000000Z
DTSTART:20270709T060000Z
DTEND:20270709T100000Z
SUMMARY:Hardrock 100
DESCRIPTION:100-mile endurance run with 33\,441 feet of climb and 33\,441 feet of descent (66\,882 feet total elevation change). Average elevation 11\,186 feet\, with low point at 7\,680 feet (Ouray) and high point at 14\,048 feet (Handies Peak). Course runs counter-clockwise direction. Lottery-based entry system with qualifying requirements. Race includes scholarship opportunities and volunteer positions.
LOCATION:Silverton\, Colorado
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pikes-peak-ultra-2027@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20261101T000000Z
DTSTART:20270724T053000Z
DTEND:20270724T093000Z
SUMMARY:Pikes Peak Ultra
DESCRIPTION:Pikes Peak Ultra is an ultramarathon event featuring multiple distance options (20K\, 30K\, 50K\, and 50 Mile) starting at Bear Creek Regional Park in Colorado Springs. The course winds through stunning trails including High Drive\, Cheyenne Canon\, Seven Bridges Trail\, and Pipeline Trail\, with much of the course on crushed granite. The 50K and 50 Mile options include a summit of Mt. Rosa with panoramic city views. All runners receive a custom race shirt\, BOCO trucker hat\, and finishers' medal.
LOCATION:Bear Creek Regional Park\, 21st and Argus Blvd\, Colorado Springs\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:leadville-trail-100-mtb-2027@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20261101T000000Z
DTSTART:20270814T060000Z
DTEND:20270814T100000Z
SUMMARY:Leadville Trail 100 MTB
DESCRIPTION:The Life Time Leadville Trail 100 MTB is one of the most prestigious endurance cross-country mountain bike events in the world. Riders tackle a grueling 100-mile course with approximately 12\,000 feet of elevation gain\, starting at 10\,152 feet and reaching a peak elevation of 12\,500 feet at Columbine Mine. The race is known as 'Race Across the Sky' and offers finishers the coveted silver and gold beltbuckle. Lottery registration opens December 1-15\, 2026 with results announced January 6\, 2027. Entry fee: $575.
LOCATION:135 E 6th Street\, Leadville\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:leadville-trail-100-run-2027@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20261101T000000Z
DTSTART:20270821T040000Z
DTEND:20270821T080000Z
SUMMARY:Leadville Trail 100 Run
DESCRIPTION:The Life Time Leadville Trail 100 RUN presented by La Sportiva is one of the oldest and most storied endurance running events in the world. This brutal out-and-back ultramarathon starts and finishes in Leadville with steep climbs\, high-altitude passes\, and technical terrain on the Colorado Trail. The course features two climbs over Hope Pass at 12\,500 feet elevation. Entry is by lottery.
LOCATION:Corner of 6th St & Harrison\, Leadville\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:telluride-mountain-run-2027@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20261101T000000Z
DTSTART:20270828T050000Z
DTEND:20270828T090000Z
SUMMARY:Telluride Mountain Run
DESCRIPTION:Trail running event in Telluride\, Colorado with three race distance options
LOCATION:Telluride\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:the-grand-traverse-run-2027@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20261101T000000Z
DTSTART:20270904T060000Z
DTEND:20270904T100000Z
SUMMARY:The Grand Traverse Run
DESCRIPTION:The Grand Traverse Mountain Run is a point-to-point ultramarathon from Crested Butte to Aspen\, Colorado. Runners travel 40 miles across the Elk Mountains with over 6\,000 feet of elevation gain. The course follows the route of the Grand Traverse Backcountry Ski race. This fundraising event is operated by Crested Butte Nordic\, a 501(c)(3) recreational non-profit organization. General registration opens December 1st\, 2026 at midnight.
LOCATION:Town Park\, Crested Butte\, CO to Ajax Park – 1001 S. Ute Ave\, Aspen\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pikes-peak-marathon-2027@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20261101T000000Z
DTSTART:20270918T080000Z
DTEND:20270918T120000Z
SUMMARY:Pikes Peak Marathon
DESCRIPTION:The Pikes Peak Marathon\, founded in 1956\, is the oldest continually held marathon in the United States. It takes runners from Manitou Springs\, Colorado\, to the summit of Pikes Peak at 14\,115 feet and back down for a total of 26.2 grueling mountain miles\, climbing approximately 7\,800 vertical feet up the historic Barr Trail. The sister race\, the Pikes Peak Ascent\, is a 13.3-mile climb to the summit.
LOCATION:441 Manitou Ave\, Suite 100\, Manitou Springs\, CO 80829
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:snow-mountain-ranch-trail-running-festival-2027@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20261101T000000Z
DTSTART:20270918T063000Z
DTEND:20270918T103000Z
SUMMARY:Snow Mountain Ranch Trail Running Festival
DESCRIPTION:The 13th annual Snow Mountain Ranch Trail Running Festival features 5 races on wide open Nordic tracks at the YMCA of the Rockies. Courses are 100% dirt terrain with stunning views of changing colors\, rolling hills\, and picturesque landscapes. Races include a 50K (31.4 miles\, 4\,236 ft elevation gain)\, 33K (20.2 miles\, 2\,443 ft elevation gain)\, Half Marathon (12.8 miles\, 1\,707 ft elevation gain)\, 10K\, and 5K. Registration closes September 13\, 2027 at 11:59 PM MT.
LOCATION:1101 County Rd 53\, Granby\, CO 80446
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR